-- title:
--   Transport of a crossing presentation to the base change over O
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and the intermediate field $K$ of $L \subset L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image the coefficient embedding of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157); write $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) with structure map $\pi =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, and let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, equipped with closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ into the base change $X_k = X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} k$, whose images together cover $X_k$, with $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ reduced and of cardinality $n > 0$, and with $C_1, C_2$ integral. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with uniformiser $\varpi$, $\rho_O : A \to O$ an injective ring homomorphism and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to k$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$ the structure map $A \to k$, and let $\mathrm{bc} : X_k \to X_O := X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} O$ be a morphism commuting with the projections to $X$ and compatible with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{to}\kappa)$ on the second factors. Let $\nu$ be a point of $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$, let $x \in X$ be its image under the composite $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2 \to C_1 \to X_k \to X$ and $x_\nu \in X_O$ its image under that composite with $\mathrm{bc}$ in place of $X_k \to X$, and assume the generic points of $C_1$ and of $C_2$ have images in $X$ specialising to $x$ (hypotheses $h_1$, $h_2$) and images in $X_O$ specialising to $x_\nu$ (hypotheses $h_{O,1}$, $h_{O,2}$). Finally let $\varpi_A$ be a uniformiser of $A$, and let $u, v$ in the stalk $R = \mathcal{O}_{X,x}$ generate the branch ideals of $h_1$ and of $h_2$ respectively — the branch ideal of a specialisation $\xi \rightsquigarrow y$ being the preimage of the maximal ideal of the stalk at $\xi$ under the specialisation map of stalks — with the sum of these two ideals equal to the maximal ideal of $R$ and with $u v = c \cdot \varpi_A$ in $R$ for some unit $c$, where $\varpi_A$ is taken to $R$ through $\pi$ on global sections followed by the germ map. Then there exist $e \ge 1$ and $g, h$ in the stalk $S = \mathcal{O}_{X_O, x_\nu}$ such that $g h = \varpi^e$ in $S$ (with $\varpi$ transported to $S$ through the second projection on global sections followed by the germ map), the maximal ideal of $S$ is generated by $\varpi$, $g$ and $h$, and $g$ lies in the branch ideal of $h_{O,1}$ while $h$ lies in the branch ideal of $h_{O,2}$.
--
--   This is the descent-free transport of a normal crossing presentation at a singular point of the special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ from the base $A = \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[\zeta_p]$ to a coefficient discrete valuation ring $O$ above it, the ramification index $e$ of $\rho_O$ appearing in the relation $gh = \varpi^e$. It feeds the construction of oriented étale crossing charts for the base-changed model, used in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart_baseChange_of_injective_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart_baseChange_of_injective_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
